From 904fa0c8aa8bfc62381481524c51c641e5ddae85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cary Palmer <24235924+professorpalmer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:38:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] server: report reasoning tokens and a budget force-close; a
 per-request budget raises the output cap

A client could only see a force-close by finding the budget message inside reasoning_content.
The reasoning-budget sampler now counts the tokens it accepts inside reasoning blocks and records
when the budget (not a manual reasoning_end) forced the end sequence. The final response carries
both: timings.reasoning_n, timings.reasoning_budget_exhausted, and
usage.completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens (OpenAI field), streaming and non-streaming, only
when the request ran with a budget sampler.

With --reasoning-max-tokens-floor on, a per-request reasoning_budget_tokens above the server
budget moves the floor to budget + 4096, and a request with no output cap gets that floor as
n_predict instead of the server default -n. Before, a client that sent a 40960 budget and no
max_tokens was cut off at -n inside its thinking.

Tests: test-reasoning-budget covers the report (natural end, exhaustion, clone/reset, manual
force, budget 0, re-armed blocks, null sampler). Live check on Qwen3.5-2B (CPU):
bench/budget_report_probe.py in bonsai-ada-surgery, 4/4.

Resolved onto the Yamadori series (this is bonsai-ada-surgery 0035, MIT, Cary Palmer): it conflicts with our 0034 reasoning-budget nudge in
common/reasoning-budget.cpp/.h and tests/test-reasoning-budget.cpp. Kept both: the report counts the NUDGING state's forced tokens as reasoning,
the path where the nudge spends the budget (end sequence forced) sets `exhausted`, the new fields follow the nudge's in the struct, init and reset,
and test_reasoning_budget_report_nudge covers the combination.
